# No absolute paths in `.clangd*`

**Hard rule.** `.clangd`, `.clangd.template`, and every nested
`**/.clangd` must use **repo-relative** (or file-relative) `-I` / `--sysroot`
paths only. Never `/home/...`, `/Users/...`, drive letters, or
`@@ROOT@@` → absolute expansion.

## Why

Checkout-absolute paths make the IDE config machine-specific, dirty diffs,
and fight the owner's reading/search. Relative paths resolve against the
directory of the `.clangd` file that contains them (clangd).

## How

| File | Paths relative to |
|------|-------------------|
| package-root `.clangd` / `.clangd.template` | package root (`-Iexp2/...`, `-Isrc/...`, `-I.`) |
| nested module `.clangd` (e.g. `fs/littlefs/`, `net/`, `boot/.../bios/`) | that file's directory (`-I.`, `-Ivendor`, `-I../../libc`) |

`scripts/setup.d/deps/ide.sh` **copies** templates; it must not `sed` in
`${ROOT}` / absolute `-I`.

## Allowed absolute paths (not `.clangd`)

`build/compile_commands.json` may still use absolute `directory` / `file`
entries — that is a separate CDB indexing constraint. Do not "fix" that
by putting abs `-I` into `.clangd`.

## Verify after edits

```
rg -n '/home/|/Users/|[A-Za-z]:\\\\|@@ROOT@@' .clangd .clangd.template \
  tests/host/.clangd tests/host/.clangd.template \
  exp2 -g '*.clangd'
```

Must return nothing.
